{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve the supplied staged help content on TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service listened on 0.0.0.0:8080 and returned HTTP 200 for the nested help file with content exactly matching the staged SHA-256 checksum, both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-7ef065dc618843e1","cmd-5dddf66cae1c4cfd","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Permanently redirect old /manual URLs to corresponding /help URLs while preserving the remaining path and query string.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Representative root and nested legacy URLs returned HTTP 301 with the corresponding /help path and unchanged query parameters. Nested redirect behavior was observed again after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7ef065dc618843e1","cmd-db6598c0a55d4253","cmd-5dddf66cae1c4cfd"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Continue serving the supplied /status.txt document directly, without redirecting it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Requests to /status.txt, including requests with query strings, returned HTTP 200 and content exactly matching the supplied status document before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-7ef065dc618843e1","cmd-db6598c0a55d4253","cmd-5dddf66cae1c4cfd"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64. The implementation used the already-installed Python 3.9 runtime and recovered successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-887a8ee18f7145bf","cmd-ab2102f323f14c80","cmd-5dddf66cae1c4cfd","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.91,"summary":"The required service, dedicated account, firewall opening, and reboot had clear task or evidence roles. The node finished with no failed services and healthy package-manager state. Two minor hygiene issues occurred: the service was briefly activated using the special nobody account before that unsafe configuration was reverted and replaced with the dedicated help-site account (cmd-f6dda75d052a46de, cmd-958dc1b06a924af3, corrected by cmd-380d872528e744a7); and seven bounded verification artifacts remained in /tmp instead of being cleaned up—help-served.html, status-served.txt, status-headers.txt, pre-status.txt, post-help.html, post-status.txt, and post-status.headers—created by cmd-7ef065dc618843e1, cmd-db6598c0a55d4253, and cmd-5dddf66cae1c4cfd. The former was reverted; the temporary-file residue remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f6dda75d052a46de","cmd-958dc1b06a924af3","cmd-380d872528e744a7","cmd-7ef065dc618843e1","cmd-db6598c0a55d4253","cmd-5dddf66cae1c4cfd","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, an acknowledged scheduled reboot, a changed boot identity, and recovered service, content, redirect, firewall, and platform state. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity change.","limitations":["HTTP behavior was tested through node1's managed IP from node1 itself rather than from an independently captured remote client.","Only representative root and nested legacy URLs were behaviorally tested; the captured handler implementation supports the broader /manual path family, but every possible path was not probed."]}
